WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.700
When did someone last try to
break our website on our behalf?

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.150
It is a front door that
anyone on earth can knock on.

00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:08.515
Four ways in.

00:00:09.817 --> 00:00:12.547
First, a search box that
talks to the database.

00:00:13.022 --> 00:00:15.032
Every form takes text from a stranger.

00:00:15.547 --> 00:00:19.117
If the code does not keep what the
visitor typed apart from commands,

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.477
the visitor can type instructions.

00:00:21.982 --> 00:00:25.192
The whole customer database
can leave in one request.

00:00:25.607 --> 00:00:30.597
The GDPR requires notifying
the regulator within 72 hours.

00:00:31.717 --> 00:00:33.807
Second, the plugin everyone forgot.

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:38.372
A website is a content system,
plugins, a theme and libraries,

00:00:38.802 --> 00:00:40.412
each written by someone else.

00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:41.907
When a hole is found,

00:00:42.157 --> 00:00:45.187
the fix and the description of
the hole are published together.

00:00:45.487 --> 00:00:48.527
Scanners then sweep the internet
for sites on the old version,

00:00:48.527 --> 00:00:50.457
and find them in hours.

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:55.067
Third, customer accounts opened
with someone else's leak.

00:00:55.327 --> 00:00:56.577
People reuse passwords.

00:00:57.222 --> 00:01:00.532
A bot network tries leaked
pairs against our login page,

00:01:00.842 --> 00:01:02.592
millions of attempts a night.

00:01:02.882 --> 00:01:07.312
The result is fraud on our site,
refunds we pay, and a headline about us.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.900
Fourth, our page, their code.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:13.840
Checkout and login pages load
scripts from other companies.

00:01:14.265 --> 00:01:16.815
Those scripts can read
every field on the page.

00:01:17.165 --> 00:01:18.795
If one supplier is compromised,

00:01:19.365 --> 00:01:20.455
the script is swapped,

00:01:21.085 --> 00:01:24.015
payments still succeed,
and card numbers go elsewhere.

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:26.427
What good looks like.

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:28.002
The payment card standard,

00:01:28.792 --> 00:01:30.922
version 4.0.1,

00:01:31.052 --> 00:01:35.982
requirements 6.4.3 and 11.6.1,

00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:40.882
requires an inventory of scripts on
payment pages, and tamper detection.

00:01:41.272 --> 00:01:43.422
Safe code, and a yearly pentest.

00:01:43.727 --> 00:01:45.277
Patches land within days.

00:01:45.657 --> 00:01:48.127
Customers log in with a second factor.

00:01:49.963 --> 00:01:51.173
A suggested first step.

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:54.608
Ask when someone last tried to
break the site on our behalf.

00:01:54.953 --> 00:01:57.903
And who is paged, by name,
when it breaks for real.

00:01:59.483 --> 00:02:02.873
The website is the one system
every attacker can reach.

00:02:03.193 --> 00:02:04.403
Test it on purpose.

